2026-09-03T14:59Z Minh Ha-Duong created

--- body ---
## Context

Ticket 0625 (PR #295) wrapped every real adapter's process spawn with
`Posture.wrap()` so no target runs under the operator's identity. Round-1
review found one adapter (`zotero_mcp.py`) had an unwrapped live spawn
(`install()`'s `pip install` step) despite `running()` being correctly
wrapped — the class of defect this ticket exists to catch before it recurs.
Only `beaver.py` and `zotero_mcp.py` got a dedicated
`test_running_refuses_before_spawning_when_the_posture_is_unavailable`-style
test (round-1 finding #6, round-2 finding #9 in PR #295's review). `zotseek.py`,
`zotero_core_6012.py`, and `zoteus.py` were verified correct by code reading
only — a future edit moving a `wrap()` call after its `Popen`/`Server` call in
any of those three would go undetected by the suite.

## Relevant files

- `bench/acceptance/adapters/zotseek.py` — no posture-refusal test
- `bench/acceptance/adapters/zotero_core_6012.py` — no posture-refusal test
- `bench/acceptance/adapters/zoteus.py` — no adapter test file at all (pre-existing gap, not introduced by 0625)
- `tests/test_acceptance_adapter_beaver.py` — the existing pattern to mirror
- `tests/test_acceptance_adapter_zotero_mcp.py` — the existing pattern to mirror (covers the `Server`-shaped spawn)

## Actions

1. Add `test_running_refuses_before_spawning_when_the_posture_is_unavailable`
   (or equivalent) for `zotseek.py` and `zotero_core_6012.py`, mirroring
   `beaver.py`'s direct-`Popen` shape test.
2. For `zoteus.py`: either add a minimal adapter test file mirroring
   `zotero_mcp.py`'s `Server`-shaped test, or fold a posture-refusal case into
   wherever `zoteus.py` first gets test coverage.

## Test

Each new test asserts that a refused `Posture` (account absent/non-working)
causes `running()` to raise before any `Popen`/`Server` construction — same
shape as the two existing tests.

## Verification
- [ ] all five real adapters have a posture-refusal test
- [ ] `make check` green

## Invariants
- No change to `posture.py`'s mechanism — this is test coverage only.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `zotseek`, `zotero_core_6012`, `zoteus` each covered by a posture-refusal test
